PROJECT

A Romanian grammatical error correction (GEC) system with a two-phase architecture.
Phase 1 detects erroneous tokens; phase 2 rewrites the flagged spans. The project
was built for the SSL and NLP master's courses and follows the approach of Tudose,
Ruseti, and Dascalu (2025), "Show Me All Writing Errors: A Two-Phased Grammatical
Error Corrector for Romanian", Information 16, 242.


ARCHITECTURE

Phase 1 is a RoBERT-large encoder with two classification heads on top of every
subword. The binary head decides whether the token is erroneous. The 7-class head
predicts the error type (no_change, diacritics, spelling, orthographic, punctuation,
morphology, agreement). Token-level predictions are propagated up to the word
level via the first-subword-of-each-word rule.

Phase 2 is a mT5-base sequence-to-sequence model. Erroneous spans flagged by
phase 1 are wrapped in typed tags (for example <e_diac> and </e_diac> around a
diacritics span), and the resulting tagged sentence is given to mT5-base. The
model generates a corrected sentence; tokens not inside any tagged span are
mostly copied through.

Two stages are optional. A language-model rescoring step (RoGPT2-medium) can
rerank the corrector's top-k beam candidates. A self-supervised pretraining
track (DAE over RoBERT-large) produces a checkpoint that can be substituted for
the supervised detector's base model in a separate experiment. Neither is
required for the canonical pipeline.


DIRECTORY STRUCTURE

src/
  utils.py                     tokenization, alignment, span-tag vocabulary
  data_prep.py                 CSV to JSONL conversion for training
  detector.py                  phase 1 training
  seq2seq.py                   phase 2 training
  pipeline.py                  end-to-end inference
  eval.py                      evaluation on real Romanian datasets
  eval_syn.py                  evaluation on the synthetic test split
  errant_eval.py               ERRANT span-based F0.5 scoring
  sweep_threshold.py           detector threshold sweep
  sweep_lambda.py              rescoring lambda sweep
  demo_interactive.py          interactive terminal demo
  ssl_corruption.py            DAE corruption module (teammate-owned)
  ssl_trainer.py               DAE pretraining (teammate-owned)
  ssl_trainer_safe.py          thin wrapper that fixes a save_pretrained issue
  prepare_unlabeled_corpus.py  unlabeled text extraction (teammate-owned)
scripts/                       SLURM batch and interactive scripts
data/
  synthetic.csv                training data (input)
  prepared/                    train/val/test JSONL produced by prep
results/                       training and evaluation outputs
slurm_outs/                    captured SLURM stdout/stderr
download_models.py             prefetch HuggingFace models
Makefile                       local and cluster orchestration


REQUIREMENTS

The project runs on the FEP HPC cluster with SLURM. All training and evaluation
happens inside a Singularity container at $HOME/ml_general_v5.sif on the cluster,
which bundles PyTorch, transformers, datasets, spacy, errant 3.0, and the rest of
the runtime dependencies. The local side needs only ssh and tar; nothing else is
installed locally.


INSTALLATION

1. Clone the repository locally.
2. Configure ssh access to fep.grid.pub.ro using the student account issued by the
   course.
3. Ensure the singularity image ml_general_v5.sif is present at
   $HOME/ml_general_v5.sif on the cluster. The image is shared via the course's
   HPC support; copy from a teammate or request a rebuild.
4. Put the HuggingFace token at $HOME/.hf_token on the cluster (one line, no
   newline at the end).
5. Run make upload-data once to push data/synthetic.csv onto the cluster.


WORKFLOW

Code is edited locally and synced to the cluster with make upload. Every training,
evaluation, and sweep runs as an sbatch job on the cluster via Makefile targets.
Output is pulled back with make results. The typical loop is: edit locally,
make upload, ssh to fep, make <target>, watch slurm_outs/, make results.


MAKEFILE TARGETS

Local file transfer
  make upload            push code to the cluster (excludes data, models, results)
  make upload-data       push data/synthetic.csv separately
  make results           pull results/ back to local
  make download          pull repository state back

Data preparation
  make prep              CSV to JSONL, stratified split
  make prep-ssl-corpus   extract clean text for DAE pretraining (separate track)

Training (on cluster)
  make train-detector    fine-tune phase 1
  make train-seq2seq     fine-tune phase 2
  make train-ssl         DAE pretraining (separate experimental track)

Evaluation
  make eval              real datasets: CNA + RoComments, threshold 0.5 (baseline)
  make eval-rescore      real datasets with RoGPT2-medium rescoring at lambda 2.0,
                         threshold 0.3 (canonical configuration)
  make eval-syn          synthetic test split

Sweeps
  make sweep-threshold   detector threshold over a fixed grid
  make sweep-lambda      rescoring lambda at the chosen threshold

Demos
  make demo              canned five-sentence smoke test (sbatch)
  make demo-interactive  interactive terminal session (uses srun --pty)

Job management
  make status            squeue for the current user
  make cancel            cancel the most recent job


RUNNING A DEMO

After make upload, ssh into fep and run make demo-interactive. The script
allocates a GPU via srun --pty and opens an interactive prompt inside the
container. Type a Romanian sentence at the > prompt and press enter; the demo
prints the tokenization, the flagged tokens, the tagged input passed to the
corrector, and the final output. Type q (or quit, or exit) to leave; Ctrl+D
also works. Example sentences are listed below.


EXAMPLE SENTENCES

Try sentences that exercise each error category. These are illustrative; the
detector's calibration determines what is actually flagged on real input.

  diacritics:   Romania este o tara frumoasa
  spelling:     Aceasta este o popoziie buna
  agreement:    Copii a venit acasa
  morphology:   Eu mergem la magazin pentru paine
  punctuation:  Salut cum esti
  orthographic: Sa au facut atatea lucruri
  clean:        Astazi este o zi frumoasa


EVALUATING THE FULL PIPELINE

The canonical evaluation runs through make eval-rescore. It uses threshold 0.3,
RoGPT2-medium rescoring at lambda 2.0, and ERRANT F0.5 computed by emitting M2
files manually from Romanian token alignment and calling errant_compare. Results
land in results/eval_rescore/ as <dataset>_summary.json and <dataset>_samples.json.
summary.json contains exact match, changed rate, spurious rate, stayed-same rate,
and ERRANT precision/recall/F0.5. samples.json contains the first 50 examples
with the system's outputs alongside the references, for qualitative inspection.


REPRODUCING THE FULL EXPERIMENT

1. make upload-data            push the dataset
2. make download-models        cache HuggingFace models on the cluster
3. make prep                   build train/val/test JSONL
4. make train-detector         train phase 1
5. make train-seq2seq          train phase 2
6. make eval                   baseline real-data numbers
7. make eval-rescore           rescored evaluation at threshold 0.3

Steps 4 and 5 can run in parallel as separate sbatch jobs.


FILES NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY

Trained checkpoints in results/detector/ and results/seq2seq/ are produced by
the training jobs and are not committed. data/synthetic.csv is uploaded
separately via make upload-data. The HuggingFace cache at $HF_HOME on the
cluster fills as models are downloaded; it is not part of this repository.

